// Cloudflare deployment for the PUBLIC (snapshot-mode) dashboard. The design is
// docs/PUBLIC-DASHBOARD.md; the runbook is docs/OPERATIONS.md, "Public
// dashboard". The private dashboard is unaffected — it is still the same bundle
// served same-origin by runner/viewer over loopback.
//
// This is the INTERIM, zoneless shape. The design doc's shape — R2 behind a
// custom domain, zone cache rules carrying the TTLs, an assets-only Worker with
// no fetch handler and therefore nothing invoked in the read path — needs a
// domain on the account, and buys nothing without one: on Cloudflare, access
// control, WAF, and cache are all custom-domain features. An `r2.dev`
// development URL is world-readable to whoever learns the hostname.
//
// A gated preview needs a gate, so here there IS a `main`: one Worker serving
// the SPA from Static Assets and the published artifacts from a private bucket
// binding, with a shared secret in front of both (dashboard/worker/index.ts).
// One origin, so there is no CORS in this shape and infra/cloudflare/r2-cors.json
// does not apply to it. When the account has a domain, the read path reverts to
// the design doc's and this file loses its `main` again.
//
// Workers Static Assets rather than Pages: parity today, and Cloudflare raises
// limits on Workers first.
//
// Build before deploying — wrangler uploads `dist` as it finds it. The base is
// "/" rather than a hostname: same-origin, and the SPA appends `/v1/...` itself.
//
//   VITE_WRATHBENCH_SNAPSHOT_BASE=/ bun run --cwd dashboard build
//   bunx wrangler deploy --config dashboard/wrangler.jsonc
//
// The gate's secret is not in this file and never in argv:
//
//   bunx wrangler secret put DASHBOARD_PASSWORD --config dashboard/wrangler.jsonc
//
// The deploying shell needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN holding a token with Workers
// Scripts Edit *and* Workers R2 Storage Read (to bind the bucket). It never
// needs object write; the publisher's R2 token never needs Workers access.
{
  "name": "wrathbench-dashboard",
  "main": "./worker/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-25",
  "assets": {
    // Relative to this file: `bun run --cwd dashboard build` writes dashboard/dist.
    "directory": "./dist",
    // The SPA owns its routes (/runs, /ladder, /run/<id>, /map, ...), so a deep
    // link or a refresh must serve index.html instead of 404ing on a path that
    // only exists in the client router.
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    // `true`, not a route list: the gate has to see the page load too, or the
    // HTML is public and only the data behind it is not.
    "run_worker_first": true
  },
  "r2_buckets": [
    {
      "binding": "PUBLIC_BUCKET",
      "bucket_name": "wrathbench-public"
    }
  ],
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
